{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChU71QWjaXfXJiJoRWVGK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: approved\n\nAll four earlier scope-selection defects that this round targeted are fixed, and I found no blockers. Six low-severity follow-ups remain.\n\n## Findings\n\nAll are low severity. Each has an action, owner `@pose-maintainers` and review date 2026-12-27 in the block below.\n\n| ID | Location | Defect |\n|---|---|---|\n| N1 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go:313` | The inline comment still describes a bounded, redacted report line. |\n| N2 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:332` | A failed prefix lookup correctly fails selection, but I found no test for it in the repository. |\n| N3 | `.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md:119` | The R1 trace cites a scope-selection test, and no requirement states that naming behaviour. |\n| N4 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go:1162` | Pre-existing: changed specs with a space or non-ASCII letter in the file name are skipped silently. |\n| N5 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:133` | Pre-existing: new untracked files outside a lower root are not listed. |\n| N6 | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:251` | Carry still uses top-relative names below the top; this appears latent. |\n\n## Earlier findings\n\n| Finding | Status |\n|---|---|\n| R1-N7, R2-N1, R3-N1, R3-N2, R3-N3 | fixed |\n| R2-N3, R3-N5 | partial: see N1 |\n| R2-N2, R3-N4 | not fixed; recorded in the spec, reported as N6 and N5 |\n\n## Criteria\nAll 15 criteria passed; evidence and rationale are in the block below.\n\n## What ran\n- **Focused tests:** they passed, and `go vet` on the two packages printed nothing. The two lower-root tests fail when the round 3 `validate_scope.go` is put back.\n- **Probes:** lower, nested, spaced and non-ASCII roots selected the expected modules for tracked changes, including with `diff.relative=true`.\n- **Full validation:** both runs failed in the sandbox. The root run had 224 of 236 steps passing and the module run 221 of 233, with the same failing steps as earlier rounds. Their entries are marked passed on the sealed evidence, with the failure stated.\n- **Accepted limit:** I do not dispute L1.\n- **Cleanup:** `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal exited 0 inside the sandbox. The draft check accepted the block below.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":313,\"summary\":\"Rest of R3-N5: the inline comment at report.go:313-316 still describes a bounded line with absolute paths removed, though the note is now fixed text.\",\"action\":\"Replace the inline comment with what D1 delivers.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":332,\"summary\":\"The failed prefix lookup now fails selection (checked with a stand-in Git probe), but no test in the repository names show-prefix, so by search a regression to a silent empty prefix has no failing test.\",\"action\":\"Add a stand-in Git test that fails rev-parse --show-prefix and requires the selection error.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\",\"line\":119,\"summary\":\"The R1 trace cites TestScopeSelectionBelowADirectoryWithALeadingSpace, which exercises scope selection, not the ready-transition read of R1; no requirement or decision states the lower-root scope naming.\",\"action\":\"Trace the test to a requirement or decision that states the scope naming.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\",\"line\":1162,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing, at any root: the ready-transition listing splits on whitespace and reads quoted names, so a changed spec whose file name has a space or a non-ASCII letter is dropped with no finding (probe returned only the plain name).\",\"action\":\"List the candidates with -z and split on NUL.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":133,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing, carried from R3-N4 and recorded in the spec: below the top, a new untracked file outside the root is not listed, so nothing is selected for it (probe: changed empty).\",\"action\":\"List untracked files from the repository top and name them from the root.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\"line\":251,\"summary\":\"Carried from R2-N2 and recorded in the spec: carry exclusions and its show <head>:<path> reads are still top-relative below the top; latent because by reading carry is refused there.\",\"action\":\"Name carry reads from the root before carry runs below the top.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"}\n],\n\"prior_findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe over lower roots: changes under the root are named from it and the self-contained owner is selected, with and without diff.relative=true; TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop passes.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Probe: a tracked change outside the root is kept as ../outside.txt and selects a non-self-contained module, also with diff.relative=true.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N2\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_carry.go is unchanged; open in the spec Follow-ups; reported again as N6.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Requirements, assertion and test comment are cleaned; the inline comment at report.go:313-316 remains (N1).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_scope.go pins -c diff.relative=false; probe with diff.relative=true selects the owner of mod/x.txt; the test fails with the round 3 validate_scope.go overlaid.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N2\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"scopeRootPrefix trims only the newline and returns the error; the leading-space test passes and fails with the round 3 file overlaid; a stand-in probe shows the selection failing with Git message. Test gap is N2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N3\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Probe with root a/b: a/c/f.txt is named ../c/f.txt and the declared dependency ../c selects the module; a top file is ../../z.txt.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N4\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Probe still returns changed empty for an untracked outside file; recorded as a spec follow-up; reported as N5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R3-N5\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"The function and test comments are fixed in db5b95bf..0cad568a; git grep still finds One line, bounded at report.go:313 (N1).\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"The round 4 delta line by line and the nine code files of the range as they bear on R1-R5: ready transitions, report note and warning, scope diff, prefix, naming and untracked listing, carry consumers, the amended spec; focused tests and go vet, a round 3 overlay, probes over lower, nested, spaced and non-ASCII roots, diff.relative, prefix failure and odd spec names, and every planned pose tool including both validate runs.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Verified by probe that the diff output form is now pinned and the prefix is taken whole. Carry staying off below the top is