k accepted the block below.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"approved\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":313,\"summary\":\"Rest of R3-N5: the inline comment at report.go:313-316 still describes a bounded line with absolute paths removed, though the note is now fixed text.\",\"action\":\"Replace the inline comment with what D1 delivers.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":332,\"summary\":\"The failed prefix lookup now fails selection (checked with a stand-in Git probe), but no test in the repository names show-prefix, so by search a regression to a silent empty prefix has no failing test.\",\"action\":\"Add a stand-in Git test that fails rev-parse --show-prefix and requires the selection error.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\",\"line\":119,\"summary\":\"The R1 trace cites TestScopeSelectionBelowADirectoryWithALeadingSpace, which exercises scope selection, not the ready-transition read of R1; no requirement or decision states the lower-root scope naming.\",\"action\":\"Trace the test to a requirement or decision that states the scope naming.\",\"owner\":\"@pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-27\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\",\"line\":1162,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing, at any root: the ready-transition listing splits on whitespace and reads quoted names, so a changed spec whose file name has a space or a non-ASCII letter is dropped with no finding (probe returned only the plain name).\",\"action\":\"List the candidat